<Legal
    title="Refund policy"
    description="What is refunded on a Sikemux paid plan, what is not, and how to ask."
    updated="16 November 2026">
    <p>
        Sikemux is free, and so is a Sikemux account. This policy covers the paid plans that add to an account. Paid
        plans are not on sale yet; this is the policy they open with.
    </p>
    <p>
        Paddle sells the plans for us as the merchant of record. It takes the payment and sends the receipt, so a refund
        comes from Paddle, to the payment method you paid with.
    </p>

    <h2>The 7-day refund</h2>
    <p>
        There is no free trial. Instead, everything you pay for a plan in its first 7 days is refunded in full if you
        ask within those 7 days. You do not have to say why.
    </p>
    <p>
        The refund is given once for each plan. Buying the same plan again after a refund is not refundable.
    </p>
    <p>
        This holds for a monthly plan and a yearly one. Once you ask, the plan is not charged again, and it ends when
        the refund is paid.
    </p>

    <h2>What is not refunded</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            A renewal. You can cancel at any time before one. The plan then runs to the end of the period you paid for
            and is not charged again.
        </li>
        <li>A charge after a plan's first 7 days, such as seats you add later or a move to a larger plan.</li>
        <li>
            The rest of a period. Cancelling or deleting your account partway through does not return the time left.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to ask</h2>
    <p>
        Sign in at <a href="https://app.sikemux.com">app.sikemux.com</a>, open Plan and billing, and ask for the refund
        beside the plan. Or write to <a href="mailto:contact@nodelike.com">contact@nodelike.com</a> from the email
        address of your account.
    </p>
    <p>
        Paddle looks at each request before it pays, so the money is not back at once. If it seems stuck, write to us
        and we will chase it.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights under the law</h2>
    <p>
        This policy adds to the rights the law gives you and takes none away. In some places you have longer, such as
        the 14-day right to withdraw for people buying in the EU and the UK. <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/refund-policy">Paddle's refund policy</a> says how those rights work.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it. A payment keeps the policy it was made under.</p>
</Legal>
